  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Kvinna till Kvinna Regional Programme - Democracy and Resilience in the Western Balkans: Supporting Feminist Change Agents 2.0</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Extension of the previous 12-month project &#x201c;The Kvinna till Kvinna Regional Programme - Democracy and Resilience in the Western Balkans: Supporting Feminist Change Agents&#x201d; in 2024 (Ref: SE-ON-802401-6134-WB).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The regional programme &#x201c;The Kvinna till Kvinna Regional Programme - Democracy and Resilience in the Western Balkans: Supporting Feminist Change Agents 2.0&#x201d;, funded by FCDO and led by the Kvinna till Kvinna Foundation, is a continuation of the project &#x201c;The Kvinna till Kvinna Regional Programme - Democracy and Resilience in the Western Balkans: Supporting Feminist Change Agents&#x201d; (Ref: SE-ON-802401-6134-WB). The programme aims to address challenges in the Western Balkans related to growing nationalism, anti-democratic developments, and anti-rights movements, contributing to a shrinking civic space and negative attitudes towards gender equality, women&#x2019;s rights, and the LGBT+ community. Responding to these challenges through the support of 18 partner organisations in the region, the overarching goal is to support the improved resilience and capacity of civil society in the Western Balkans that contribute to the realisation of women&#x2019;s rights and the rights of LGBT+ persons.</narrative>
  </description>
